## Packages licensed under Apache-2.0

The dividing line is where the code runs: **everything CloudPDF ships to a browser is open source; everything that runs on a server is commercial.** The following packages are therefore licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, as set out in their own `LICENSE` files, and nothing in this document restricts them:

- `ee/engine` — `@cloudpdf/engine`, the browser client that speaks to a CloudPDF deployment over HTTPS.
- `ee/viewer/*` — `@cloudpdf/viewer` and its per-framework wrappers, the browser viewer artifacts.

Everything else under `ee/` — including `ee/server`, `ee/admin`, `ee/admin-api`, and `ee/website` — remains under the proprietary terms above. Running a CloudPDF deployment, whether hosted by CloudPDF or self-hosted, requires a separate written commercial agreement.

This license applies only to the contents of the `ee/` directory. The remainder of this repository is licensed separately (see the root `LICENSE`).

If you would like to obtain a license, please contact CloudPDF.
